* FP5 Monte Carlo / mismatch library (PERSONAL USE).
* Global (lot-to-lot) variation: use the corners in fp5.lib, or .lib fp5_mc.lib mc_global for random lots (1 sigma =
*   Vth N 24 mV / P 15 mV, Idsat ~2.1 % / 3.8 %, from 105 MOSIS C5 lots).
* Local mismatch: instance wrappers fp5n_mm / fp5p_mm (pass w, l in metres). Pelgrom single-device sigma(Vth) = A_VT/sqrt(W L):
*   A_VT N 7.7 mV um, P 11.9 mV um = Eisele et al. IEDM 1995 0.5 um measured 6.0 / 9.3 mV um scaled by oxide 141/110 A (ESTIMATE
*   of the scaling); A_beta 1.5 %um both (typical literature value, ESTIMATE).
* Each .tran/.op run in an ngspice "repeat" loop re-draws agauss(); seed with: set rndseed=<n>.
.lib mm
.param avtn=7.7e-3 avtp=11.9e-3 abeta=0.015
* ngspice BSIM3 has no delvto: Vth mismatch = random series gate offset, beta mismatch = random width scale
.subckt fp5n_mm d g s b w=10u l=1u as=0 ad=0 ps=0 pd=0
Vmm g gi dc {agauss(0, avtn/sqrt(w*l*1e12), 1)}
M1 d gi s b fp5n w={w*(1+agauss(0, abeta/sqrt(w*l*1e12), 1))} l={l} as={as} ad={ad} ps={ps} pd={pd}
.ends
.subckt fp5p_mm d g s b w=10u l=1u as=0 ad=0 ps=0 pd=0
Vmm g gi dc {agauss(0, avtp/sqrt(w*l*1e12), 1)}
M1 d gi s b fp5p w={w*(1+agauss(0, abeta/sqrt(w*l*1e12), 1))} l={l} as={as} ad={ad} ps={ps} pd={pd}
.ends
.endl mm
